cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Quantum Foundations in Lean: Finite-Dimensional Formalizations and Typed Premise Audits"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dalimier
    given-names: Bertrand
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    city: Nogent-sur-Marne
    country: FR
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2457-375X"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib library for finite-dimensional quantum foundations.
  Contains machine-checked formalizations of Naimark dilation, Wigner's theorem,
  one-directional Uhlhorn--Semrl rigidity, projective and effect-perspective
  Born representation, refinement consistency generated by elementary binary
  splits, sharpness witnesses for exposed Born-calibration premises, record and
  complexity developments, and restricted-sector stability results. Version
  1.4.1 is the publication-facing AFM audit release: it changes no theorem body
  relative to v1.4.0-journal-audit and adds an exact manuscript declaration
  audit, reviewer guide, one-command verification entry point, and refreshed
  publication/reproducibility metadata.
keywords:
  - quantum foundations
  - Born rule
  - Everett interpretation
  - refinement consistency
  - redundant records
  - Gleason theorem
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
